  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Sivelestat and Nuclear receptor coactivator 2 (NRC2) through a series of target interactions. Sivelestat is implicated in targeting the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Isoneobavachalcone and Npc168718. These compounds, in turn, are linked to NRC2, indicating a possible pathway where Sivelestat may influence NRC2 through its interaction with the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different compounds. The evidence highlights a mechanistic link involving the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta as a central mediator, though the exact role of Sivelestat in this process remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Sivelestat may modulate NRC2 through interactions with the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this mechanism.",
